{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1374114-a-chantry-in-the-middle-umbra","id":1374114,"title":"A Chantry in the Middle Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-11T06:15:56-07:00","id":1374114,"title":"A Chantry in the Middle Umbra","content":"I've got an Order of Hermes chantry, Durenmar, to be exact, that was moved into a realm in the Middle Umbra back in the day (about 40 years before Doissetep was moved to Mars). Durenmar is connected to three powerful nodes on Earth and the whole realm has been adapted by the Hermetics to ensure the chantry's security. <br /> <br /> My question is, which measures would the Hermetics have had to put in place to ensure they could keep reading and drinking tea in their Umbral chantry for a prolonged period of time, without suffering the adverse effects of lengthy Umbral stays?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12101-nitromidas","name":"Nitromidas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T06:37:29-07:00","id":1374120,"title":"","content":"No books with me atm but as far as I can recall disimbodyment (spelling?) Isn't an issue when you are in a Horizon Realm. Our group has extended that to mean any &quot;earth like&quot; realm as well. Especialy one that is created/subdued. Whether or not the RAW support this I am unsure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T07:56:26-07:00","id":1374131,"title":"","content":"That's what I've been thinking as well. Seeing as the 15th century Masters who moved the chantry likely knew what they were doing. I'm thinking they somehow &quot;anchored&quot; or &quot;grounded&quot; it, using a great circle of standing stones from Earth hidden in the forest.<br /> <br /> If you think of something else, I'd love to hear it. I'm aware of Rule 1, but I like to stay as close to RAW as possible, where possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Any technology distinguishable from magic is insufficiently advanced.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12101-nitromidas","name":"Nitromidas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T08:24:27-07:00","id":1374139,"title":"","content":"In theory, Horizon Realms protect from disembodiment because they're linked to Earth by earthly Nodes that provides the Realm with earthly Ressonance.<br /> <br /> As your Chantry receives influx from 3 Earthly Nodes, it shouldn't have any problem with this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:"